stream
BT /F2 13 Tf 56 768 Td (Cloud Backup Options for Hollins & Pryce) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 754 Td (IT5005 Information Systems Infrastructure - Assessment 2 Technical Report) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 730 Td (Candidate 0000) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 56 690 Td (1. Executive Summary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 676 Td (Hollins & Pryce, a 25-person accounting firm, currently relies on a weekly backup to an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 662 Td (external USB drive that is taken off site by one of the partners. This arrangement leaves up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 648 Td (to a week of work unprotected, depends on a single person and provides no protection against) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 634 Td (ransomware that encrypts both the server and a connected drive. This report analyses the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 620 Td (firm's backup requirements, considers cloud backup options and evaluates them against five) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 606 Td (criteria: security, recovery capability, compliance, ease of management and cost. The report) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 592 Td (recommends adopting a managed cloud backup service, referred to here as Option A \(a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 578 Td (business-tier, image-based backup service with immutable storage hosted in a UK data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 564 Td (centre\). Option A meets every mandatory requirement, supports hourly backups of the file) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 550 Td (server and database, and costs approximately GBP 3,420 per year, which is modest compared with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 536 Td (the potential cost of losing client records.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 56 496 Td (2. Requirements Analysis) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 482 Td (The requirements were derived from a review of the firm's current infrastructure and an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 468 Td (informal discussion of the partners' priorities as described in the scenario. The firm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 454 Td (operates one Windows file server holding approximately 1.2 TB of documents and a SQL-based) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 440 Td (client accounting database of around 80 GB. Data grows at roughly 15% per year, so any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 426 Td (solution must comfortably accommodate 2 TB within three years.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 402 Td (Two recovery objectives are central to backup planning [1]. The recovery point objective) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 388 Td (\(RPO\) is the maximum amount of data, measured in time, that the business can afford to lose.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 374 Td (For an accounting firm handling tax submissions with fixed deadlines, losing a week of work) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 360 Td (is unacceptable; an RPO of no more than four hours is required during the working day. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 346 Td (recovery time objective \(RTO\) is the maximum acceptable time to restore service. Staff can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 332 Td (work on local copies for a short period, so an RTO of eight hours for the full server and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 318 Td (one hour for individual files is appropriate.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 294 Td (Security and compliance requirements are significant. Accountants hold personal and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 280 Td (financial data about clients and must comply with UK GDPR, which requires appropriate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 266 Td (technical measures to protect personal data, including encryption and the ability to restore) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 252 Td (availability in a timely manner [2]. Backups must therefore be encrypted in transit and at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 238 Td (rest, and data should remain in the UK or another jurisdiction with adequate data protection) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 224 Td (arrangements. Professional bodies also expect client records to be retained for at least six) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 210 Td (years, so the solution must support long-term retention.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 186 Td (Finally, ransomware is now one of the most common causes of data loss for small businesses) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 172 Td ([3]. The solution must keep backup copies that cannot be altered or deleted by an attacker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 158 Td (who compromises the office network, a property often described as immutability. Because the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 144 Td (firm has no dedicated IT staff and relies on a part-time external contractor, the solution) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 130 Td (must also be simple to manage and must alert someone automatically when a backup fails.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 106 Td (The evaluation criteria are therefore: \(1\) security, including encryption and immutability;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 92 Td (\(2\) recovery capability against the RPO and RTO; \(3\) compliance, including UK data residency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 56 78 Td (and six-year retention; \(4\) ease of management; and \(5\) cost over three years.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 290 30 Td (Page 1 of 4) Tj ET
endstream
